TraceJVM (Shiklo fork, 2026-10-30): javac's options, notes and message text. Compiler.setOptions takes javac's options
(one per line: -Xlint:all, -g, -parameters, --enable-preview ...), stored as javac's own option processing stores them
(its Arguments needs classes TeaVM's class library lacks); the compiler had none. After compiling, the deferred
diagnostics are reported, as javac does when it closes ("Note: Main.java uses unchecked or unsafe operations.").
Diagnostics carry javac's own text: the rich formatter's message (simple class names, "where E is a type-variable"
clauses), the lint category ("[rawtypes] "), and mandatory warnings as warnings.

